1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software": the contents of the repository
   https://github.com/danigio15/gdanav — the gdanav app, the gdanav_core
   engine, the gdanav Home Assistant integration, the relay and the routing
   server configuration — with their source code, assets, documentation and
   the packages built from them, including those distributed through
   application stores.

   "Owner": Giovanni d'Aniello, the author of the Software and the holder of
   its copyright.

   "Distributor": CRV IMMOBILIARE S.R.L., which, by agreement with the Owner,
   distributes the Software and sells its paid features.

   "Repository": the repository named above.

   "You": the individual or legal entity using the Software or exercising the
   permissions of this license.

   "Authorized installer": anyone who has been given written access to the
   installer program by the Distributor.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Subject to Your compliance with this license, the Owner grants You a
   non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable and royalty-free permission to:

   (a) install and use the Software — the app on devices You own or control,
       the integration on Home Assistant instances You own or administer —
       for Your personal needs or those of Your business;

   (b) download and read the source code, in order to check what the Software
       does with Your vehicle, Your location and Your data;

   (c) modify Your installed copy for Your own use, provided that the modified
       copy is neither distributed nor made available to anyone else, and
       provided that Section 3(e) is respected;

   (d) if You are an Authorized installer, install, configure and support the
       Software for Your customers, under the conditions the Distributor has
       given You in writing.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Except as permitted by Sections 2 and 4 or by mandatory law, You may not:

   (a) redistribute, publish, mirror, re-upload, install for others or
       otherwise make the Software, or any part of it, available to third
       parties, in source or built form, modified or not, for a fee or free of
       charge;

   (b) publish the Software, or an app or integration derived from it, to an
       application store, a package repository, a HACS repository or a
       similar distribution channel;

   (c) fork, republish or otherwise reproduce the Repository as a separate
       public copy, except as permitted by Section 4;

   (d) distribute derivative works, adaptations, translations, re-branded or
       modified versions of the Software;

   (e) remove, alter, obscure or circumvent the copyright and license notices
       and attributions contained in or produced by the Software — including
       those required by the map and charging data sources listed in
       Section 7; circumvent, disable or falsify the checks on paid features
       (licenses, gift codes, subscriptions); or present the Software, or any
       part of it, as not originating from the Owner;

   (f) sublicense, sell, rent or lease the Software, or include it in a paid
       product, in a service hosted for others or in a commercial
       installation, integration or support offering — including operating
       the relay or the routing server for others — except as Section 2(d)
       permits Authorized installers;

   (g) use the names "gdanav" and "gdahome", the Software's logo or marks, or
       any confusingly similar name, to identify a derivative, a competing
       product or a service.

   This Section does not restrict acts that the law permits notwithstanding a
   contract, such as decompilation for interoperability under Articles 64-ter
   and 64-quater of Italian Law No. 633 of 22 April 1941.

4. FORKS AND CONTRIBUTIONS

   For as long as the Repository is public on GitHub, GitHub's Terms of
   Service give anyone the technical ability to view and fork it. That
   technical ability does not, by itself, grant any right to use, keep or
   publish the copy so created. Accordingly, for as long as the Repository is
   public:

   (a) a fork is permitted only as the technical means of preparing a
       contribution to be submitted to the Repository as a pull request;

   (b) such a fork must not be modified beyond what the contribution
       requires, must not be advertised, distributed or presented as an
       independent project, and must be deleted once the pull request has
       been merged or closed;

   (c) any other use of a fork, including simply keeping it public as a
       standalone copy of the Software, is a distribution and is prohibited
       by Section 3.

   By submitting a contribution to the Repository, You grant the Owner a
   perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free and sublicensable license
   to use, modify, publish and distribute that contribution as part of the
   Software, under this license or any other license the Owner chooses, and
   You confirm that You have the right to grant it.

5. PAID FEATURES

   Some features of the Software (gdanav Premium) are paid, and they are sold
   by the Distributor: from the app, through Apple's App Store and Google
   Play and under those stores' terms, or with gift codes. gdahome Premium
   includes gdanav Premium. An entitlement to a paid feature applies to the
   account it was purchased with, or to the home when it comes from gdahome
   Premium; it is not transferable and does not enlarge the permissions of
   Section 2. The Owner and the Distributor may add, change or withdraw paid
   features; an entitlement already granted remains valid for what it
   provided when it was granted.

6. TERMINATION

   The permissions of Section 2 terminate automatically if You breach this
   license. From then on You must stop using the Software and delete every
